 // ===== Section A: Agent A, phase 2 ==========================================
+//
+// Contracts (ABI-SPEC and STUBS-SPEC section 15), each checked where the body
+// is written:
+//   - Pool loads have exactly the two shapes of ABI-SPEC 6.2, which
+//     InstructionPattern::DecodeLoadWordFromPool accepts:
+//       ld dst,off(pp)                         offset < 32 KiB
+//       addis X,pp,ha(off) ; ld dst,lo(off)(X) X = dst, or TMP if dst is R0
+//   - LoadObject never clobbers TMP or TMP2, except LoadObject(R0, obj) with
+//     a far pool slot, which needs TMP as the base (r0 is never a base).
+//     null, true and false come from NULL_REG without the pool (STUBS-SPEC
+//     15 #11); Thread-cached objects from THR; Smis are immediates.
+//   - Dart calls through a Code object (ABI-SPEC 4.1):
+//       JIT: ld r28,idx(PP) ; li r0,entry-1 ; ldx r0,r28,r0 ; mtctr r0 ; bctrl
+//       AOT: the same with TMP in place of r28. CODE_REG is allocatable and
+//            may hold a live value across a call to a register-preserving
+//            shared stub in AOT, and r0 cannot be the base of the entry
+//            load; ARM64 uses LR here, RISC-V TMP. So an AOT BranchLink
+//            clobbers TMP (and r0, CTR, LR).
+//   - Frames (ABI-SPEC 3.1): EnterDartFrame (JIT) =
+//       mflr r0 ; stdu r31,-16(r1) ; std r0,8(r1) ; mr r31,r1 ;
+//       stdu r28,-8(r1) ; addi r0,r30,1 ; stdu r0,-8(r1) ;
+//       li r0,pool_off-1 ; ldx r30,r28,r0 ; addi r30,r30,-1 ; addi r1,r1,-n
+//     and sets constant_pool_allowed(true); LeaveDartFrame =
+//       ld r30,-16(r31) ; addi r30,r30,-1 ; mr r1,r31 ; ld r0,8(r1) ;
+//       ld r31,0(r1) ; addi r1,r1,16 ; mtlr r0
+//     and disallows the pool. AOT frames have neither the code nor the PP
+//     slot, as on ARM64.
+//   - WRITE_BARRIER_STATE (r27) holds Thread::write_barrier_mask unmodified
+//     (ABI-SPEC Amendment A5; no RISC-V xori).
+//   - MonomorphicCheckedEntryJIT/AOT emit exactly STUBS-SPEC section 8 and
+//     assert its sizes (entry offsets JIT 12/76, AOT 12/32).
 
